{title: Come Forth! Come On, with Solemn Song!}
{artist: Christian Friedrich Heinrich Sachse · tr. Jane Laurie Borthwick}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
Come forth! come on, with solemn song! The road is short, the
rest is long! The Lord brought here, He calls away:
Make no delay, This home was for a passing day.

Verse 2
Here in an inn a stranger dwelt, Here joy and grief by
turns he felt; Poor dwelling, now we close thy door!
The task is o'er, The sojourner returns no more,

Verse 3
Now of a lasting home possest, He goes to seek a
deeper rest Goodnight! the day was sultry here,
In toil and fear; Goodnight! the night is cool and clear.

Verse 4
Chime on, ye bells! again begin, And ring the Sabbath
morning in, The lab'rer's weekday work is done,
The rest begun, Which Christ hath for His people won!

Verse 5
Now open to us, gates of peace! Here let the pilgrim's
journey cease. Ye quiet slumberers, make room
In your still home, For the new stranger who has come!
